    "title": "<p>Clinicopathological and molecular features of NTRK-rearranged spindle cell neoplasms</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Rita Alaggio",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"931\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Histological pattern</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Immunophenotype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Kinases</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Age</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Site (most frequent)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Prognosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 697.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" colspan=\"6\" width=\"931\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>IF-like tumours</strong> (see <span class=\"ID-Section\"><span style=\"color: black;\">&lt;&lt;5.2.2.12&gt;&gt;</span></span><em>Infantile fibrosarcoma</em><span class=\"PageCh\"><span style=\"color: black;\">, p.&nbsp;XXX</span></span>) <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{32243019; 30585824}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 74.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 74.2pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">IF pattern</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Monomorphic spindle cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Solid/fascicular/herringbone pattern</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Haemangiopericytoma-like vascular network</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Mitoses</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Lymphocytic infiltrate</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 74.2pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Variable SMA, S100, CD34</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 74.2pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">BRAF, NTRK1, NTRK3, c-Met (MET), RET </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{28877062; 28097808; 29915264; 31994201}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 74.2pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">&lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;years, rarely older children</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 74.2pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Extremities, trunk, intra-abdominal</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 74.2pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">TBD, probably more aggressive than classic IF</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 697.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" colspan=\"6\" width=\"931\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Paediatric soft tissue tumours with kinase fusions</strong> <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{32243019}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 32.95pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 32.95pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">LFNT</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Spindle cells forming fascicles dissecting the adipose lobules in a lipofibromatosis-like pattern</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 32.95pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Variable S100</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">CD34+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">SOX10&minus;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">H3&nbsp;p.K27me3 retained</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 32.95pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">NTRK1, RET </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{31994201; 32506523; 31219820; 29892662; 27259011}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 32.95pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Children, infants (mostly with <em>RET</em> fusions), less frequently young adults</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 32.95pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Extremities, abdominal wall</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 32.95pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">TBD, perhaps favourable</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Spindle cell tumours</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">S100+/CD34+ MPNST-like primitive spindle cells in a solid/fascicular growth pattern</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Stromal/perivascular hyalinization</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">S100+, CD34+</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">SOX10&minus;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">H3&nbsp;p.K27me3 retained</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">RAF1, BRAF, NTRK1, NTRK2 <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{30276917}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Children, young adults (50% of patients aged &lt;&nbsp;18&nbsp;years)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Extremities, trunk, other sites (maxilla, stomach)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">TBD (of 5&nbsp;cases with follow-up, 1&nbsp;DOD aged 18&nbsp;years)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Spindle cell tumours with a haemangiopericytic or myopericytoma-like pattern</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">SMA+, CD34+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">NTRK1 (2&nbsp;cases)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">RET (1&nbsp;case) </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{28028925; 26863915}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">3&nbsp;children, 2&nbsp;adults</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Trunk</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">1&nbsp;AWD, 2&nbsp;ANED</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"265\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High-grade spindle cell sarcoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Variable CD34 or S100</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">NTRK3 <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{31112350}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mostly adults, 3&nbsp;children</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Extremities (1&nbsp;case), intra-abdominal (2&nbsp;cases)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">1&nbsp;DOD, 1&nbsp;AWD</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">AWD, alive with disease; ANED, alive with no evidence of disease; DOD, died of disease; IF, infantile fibrosarcoma; MPNST, malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumour; LFNT, lipofibromatosis-like neural tumour; TBD, to be defined.</p>",
